step1_tool_affordance.instruction:
The robot must carry out the task: {task}
Planned steps: {task_steps}
The selected tool is: {tool}

The image shows the tool with candidate keypoints drawn as numbered dots (1 to {n_keypoints}) and candidate direction vectors drawn as arrows labelled tau0 to tau{max_tau}.

Choose:
- Keypoint H: the GRASP point, where the two-finger gripper should close on the tool. It must lie on the handle, at a place where the gripper can close around the shaft without fouling the working head.
- Keypoint F: the FUNCTIONAL point, on the part of the tool that contacts the workpiece. For a striking tool this is the face of the head; for an edged tool the cutting edge; for a driver the tip.
- Vector tau_t: the direction in which force is applied at F during the task, pointing outward from the tool.

Choose ONLY from the numbered dots and tau labels actually drawn in the image. H and F must be different numbers.
